# docker/STATESYNC_RPC -- the RPC servers a NEW node derives its state-sync trust point from.
#
# WHAT A TRUST POINT IS. A node that starts from a snapshot does not replay the chain from the genesis: a
# CometBFT light client verifies the snapshot against a trusted (height, block hash) pair, and never looks
# at the genesis again. Whoever chooses that pair chooses the chain the new node joins.
#
# READ FROM THE CLONE, NEVER FROM network-info.txt. network-info is fetched over plain HTTP, so a trust point
# published there would be chosen by whoever sits on the path, and would walk around docker/GENESIS_SHA256.
# This file arrives with the repository, over HTTPS git, like the genesis pin, and names SERVERS rather than
# a pair: deploy/join.sh (statesync_trust_point) derives the pair at every join, over TLS --
#   1. each server's /status: its network must be the chain id the node is written with;
#   2. the trust height is the lowest head among them minus join.sh's STATESYNC_TRUST_LAG_BLOCKS;
#   3. each server's /block?height=<that height>: the same block hash from every server, or no state sync.
# A server that does not answer, or answers something unreadable, leaves the node to REPLAY from the genesis
# (said, never taken for an agreement). A server on another network, or two servers that disagree, STOP the
# join: deploy/join.sh --replay is the way past, and needs no trust point.
# Those servers are also the light client's rpc_servers (CometBFT asks for two; node-join.sh repeats a single
# one): they must serve the CometBFT JSON-RPC at the URL given, over TLS, with a certificate for that name.
#
# WHAT ONE LINE IS WORTH. With one server listed, "every server agrees" holds trivially: the anchor is then
# the TLS identity of that server's operator. It closes a man in the middle on the HTTP path; it closes
# neither a compromised operator nor a compromised certificate authority. A second server, run by someone
# else, is what turns the agreement into a witness.
#
# FORM. One URL per line: https only, a host name, an optional port and path, no query, nothing else on the
# line. join.sh refuses the whole file if one line is anything else. Comment and blank lines are ignored.
# Nothing here is specific to one genesis: the network each server serves is confronted at every join.
https://testnet-api.dendranetwork.com/rpc
